  <!-- ABOUT HERO -->
  <section id="about-hero">
    <div class="about-hero-bg"></div>
    <div class="about-hero-content">
      <p class="about-hero-eyebrow">🏔️ Est. 2025 · Nanyuki, Kenya</p>
      <h1 class="about-hero-title">
        Who We
        <em>Are</em>
      </h1>
      <div class="about-divider"></div>
      <p class="about-hero-sub">Born in the shadow of Mt. Kenya's peaks. Built by guides who grew up on these slopes. Dedicated to sharing Africa's greatest mountain with the world — one stride at a time.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- OUR STORY -->
  <section id="about-story">
    <div class="story-inner">
      <div class="story-text">
        <span class="ab-section-tag">Our Story</span>
        <h2 class="ab-section-title">Born on <em>The Mountain</em></h2>
        <div class="ab-gold-rule"></div>
        <div class="story-body">
          <p>WildStrides was founded in <strong>2025</strong> by a small team of Mt. Kenya guides, conservationists and Nanyuki-based adventure specialists who shared one conviction: that Mt. Kenya is one of the most extraordinary places on Earth — and most people have never heard of it.</p>
          <p>We set out to change that. What began as a simple guiding operation out of Nanyuki has grown into a full adventure and safari platform built entirely around the <strong>Mt. Kenya ecosystem</strong> — the mountain, its forests, its wildlife conservancies and the remarkable communities that live alongside it.</p>
          <p>Every member of our team was either born in the region or has spent years learning its trails, its wildlife and its people. We know the <strong>exact ridge where the forest opens to moorland</strong> at dawn, the waterhole where elephants drink on the Aberdare escarpment, the community ranger who tracks leopards through the cedar forest each morning.</p>
          <p>We are a young company with big ambitions — and an unshakeable commitment to making sure that <strong>every shilling spent on Mt. Kenya benefits Mt. Kenya</strong>: its conservation, its communities and its future.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="story-img-col">
        <div class="story-img-main"></div>
